{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And these are the generations of Isaac.</b> Above he explained the generations of Ishmael after the generations of the sons of Keturah; now he explains to us the generations of Isaac." "<b>Abraham begot Isaac.</b> The reason he elaborated at such length is that he did not mention here the name of his mother, as he mentioned above: 'Ishmael son of Abraham, whom Hagar bore.' And were it not so, I would say that what it writes, 'Isaac son of Abraham,' means that he raised him in his household, as we find with Moses: 'and she brought him to Pharaoh's daughter, and he became a son to her.' Therefore he repeated <b>Abraham begot Isaac</b>, to teach you that the principal offspring of Abraham is Isaac. Another interpretation: <b>Abraham begot Isaac</b> — and not Abram begot Isaac. Another interpretation: <b>Abraham begot Isaac</b> — was it only Isaac alone that he begot? Rather, the verse writes for you the one through whom Abraham was greatly exalted, as it is written: 'The crown of elders is grandchildren,' etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:50.952478547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}